# 11. R7 — Property detail UX (highest priority)

The screen should feel mature without becoming information-dense.

Recommended order:

```text
Property identity / destination
        ↓
Current share price + current state
        ↓
1Y price chart
        ↓
PBD! — mean: Platform bootstrap data
        ↓
Historical high / low / change / range
        ↓
Live market activity
        ↓
Order book / buy / sell actions
```

### PBD disclosure

Use one reusable component, e.g.:

```text
PlatformBootstrapDisclosure
```

Canonical visible text:

> **PBD! — mean: Platform bootstrap data**

It must be:

- visible on first render;
- adjacent to the historical chart/metrics;
- readable at ~480px Telegram WebView width;
- accessible;
- consistent across property detail, secondary market, charts, and bootstrap market context.

Do not bury it inside a tooltip.

### Chart UX

Optimize for a mobile/Telegram viewport:

- compact height;
- readable Y-axis values;
- sensible X-axis labels (month names rather than 52 labels);
- touch-friendly tooltip/crosshair if the existing chart library supports it;
- avoid rendering every point label;
- memoize derived chart data;
- do not refetch the entire property page on tooltip interaction;
- preserve loading/error/empty states.

### Important visual distinction

The PBD history should look like **historical context**, not a live exchange feed.

If a live series exists, clearly distinguish the post-cutoff portion.

Before first live trade:

```text
Historical price — PBD
No live trades yet
```

After first live trade:

```text
Historical price — PBD
Live market activity
```

**R7 done when:** resale property detail is materially more useful at first open and PBD disclosure is immediately visible.

