# 15. Seed commands and idempotency

Prefer separate commands:

```text
db:seed
  → canonical property/application seed

db:seed:bootstrap-history
  → PBD historical context only
```

If repository conventions require another name, follow them.

### Deterministic key

Use an equivalent unique identity:

```text
propertyId + observedAt + provenance + bootstrapVersion
```

### Reseed guarantee

Second PBD seed:

```text
same inputs → same DB state
```

PBD seed may update/prune only its own PBD version.

It must never update/delete:

```text
live trades
live orders
real holdings
real balances
real transactions
real settlements
real NFT state
```

### Production safety

Make it difficult to accidentally run a destructive PBD cleanup against live data. If the repository has environment guards, use them. If it does not, add a minimal explicit guard rather than relying on operator memory.

**R10 seed done when:** double-run tests prove exact idempotency and live-row immunity.

